---
description: CueBank notes first in every new chat; the user's word is the authority; save corrections the same turn
alwaysApply: true
---

First action in every new chat, before any reply including one-liners, clarifying questions, and task-status lines: call the CueBank tool continuity_recent. Say nothing about the task, not even a plan, status line, or question, until notes are loaded. Saved notes hold tone and format rules that apply to every reply.

- What the user says is the authority. Saved notes come next. Your own defaults come last.
- When the user states a rule, correction, preference, or decision, save it in the same turn, in their words: `continuity_add` for a new one, `continuity_update` by id when it changes a saved note. Tell them what you saved. Do not wait to be asked.
- Push back. If a request conflicts with a saved note, or looks wrong or risky, say so in one or two lines and name the note before you act.
- Be proactive. Call `continuity_search` before risky actions and whenever the task touches something that may already be decided. Then do the work. Do not just offer to do it.
- Delete a note with `continuity_delete` only when the user asks to remove or forget it.
- If a CueBank call fails, say so. Do not claim notes were loaded when they were not.
